1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,415
We’ve been looking at different types of conflicts that may arise between wildlife

2
00:00:06,415 --> 00:00:11,206
and humans at the boundaries of protected areas such as national parks

3
00:00:11,206 --> 00:00:12,850
and animal sanctuaries.

4
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:17,499
I’d like to illustrate this by telling you about some research that I’ve been

5
00:00:17,499 --> 00:00:23,229
involved in recently in the central African country of Zambia in the area around

6
00:00:23,229 --> 00:00:25,474
the Chembe Bird Sanctuary,

7
00:00:25,474 --> 00:00:28,920
which contains over three hundred of the listed birds of Zambia.

8
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:34,817
These include a number of birds of prey, such as eagles, hawks and owls,

9
00:00:34,817 --> 00:00:39,150
that live by hunting and killing other birds and animals.

10
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:43,543
Now, most of the people living in the local communities near to the bird

11
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:46,071
sanctuary are small-scale farmers,

12
00:00:46,071 --> 00:00:52,570
and these birds of prey provide important social and ecological benefits to them.

13
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:57,604
For example, a lot of damage can be caused to farmers’ crops by rodents

14
00:00:57,604 --> 00:00:58,727
such as rats,

15
00:00:58,727 --> 00:01:02,878
which would consume the crops as they grow in the fields as well as

16
00:01:02,878 --> 00:01:07,150
after harvesting if they weren’t hunted and killed by the birds.

17
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:12,830
And the predatory habits of these birds also protect farmers in other ways.

18
00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:19,549
For example, a major danger to rural workers is snakes, whose bite may be dangerous

19
00:01:19,549 --> 00:01:20,733
or even fatal,

20
00:01:20,733 --> 00:01:26,730
and birds of prey have a major role in keeping their populations under control.

21
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:32,548
Local people have always been aware of these benefits and for years, even before

22
00:01:32,548 --> 00:01:38,064
the sanctuary was opened in 1973, the birds played a key role in the

23
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:39,930
culture of the region.

24
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:47,081
However, more recently, the sanctuary and its birds have also become increasingly important to

25
00:01:47,081 --> 00:01:49,425
the community in economic terms,

26
00:01:49,425 --> 00:01:56,757
because at present, after a relatively slow start, tourism has become an important source

27
00:01:56,757 --> 00:01:58,820
of revenue for them.

28
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:04,885
However, although these birds of prey are protected by the government, their numbers are

29
00:02:04,885 --> 00:02:06,070
falling.

30
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:08,530
Some of these deaths are accidental.

31
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:13,113
Fatalities occur when birds alight on roads to catch and eat their prey,

32
00:02:13,113 --> 00:02:16,350
and are hit by fast-moving traffic.

33
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:21,654
Drivers in Zambia have to take special care at night, as birds may regard

34
00:02:21,654 --> 00:02:25,250
the quieter roads as safe places to sleep.

35
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:31,278
Accidental deaths may also occur if these birds fly close to high-voltage power lines,

36
00:02:31,278 --> 00:02:33,730
as they may be electrocuted.

37
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:38,231
This is a particular danger in the heavy rain which can occur in the

38
00:02:38,231 --> 00:02:42,250
region in the months from December to April.

39
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:46,610
And local farmers also pose a threat to these birds.

40
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:52,440
As well as growing crops, small-scale farmers in the area also rear chickens.

41
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:57,664
These provide food for the farmers’ families, as well as being an important source

42
00:02:57,664 --> 00:02:58,910
of income.

43
00:02:58,910 --> 00:03:03,418
But they’re also an easy target for birds of prey,

44
00:03:03,418 --> 00:03:06,323
and so farmers may shoot these birds,

45
00:03:06,323 --> 00:03:09,108
which is illegal but understandable,

46
00:03:09,108 --> 00:03:11,151
or they may poison the birds,

47
00:03:11,151 --> 00:03:16,260
which again is illegal and can have negative effects on the ecosystem.

48
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:21,820
So how else can farmers protect their chickens from birds of prey?

49
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:26,639
Some people believe that to prevent the predators from settling near the area where

50
00:03:26,639 --> 00:03:31,780
the chickens are kept it’s best to keep this area free from vegetation.

51
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:37,919
But in fact this is counter-productive as it means the chickens have no cover to hide in

52
00:03:37,919 --> 00:03:41,250
and they’ll be easier for the birds to see.

53
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:45,923
Another possibility would be to prevent the chickens from going outside at all,

54
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:49,754
and to keep them safe from predators inside a building,

55
00:03:49,754 --> 00:03:55,510
but this would cost far too much to be a practical solution.

56
00:03:55,510 --> 00:04:00,023
Nearly all the farmers reported that they spent a lot of time

57
00:04:00,023 --> 00:04:05,700
and effort trying to frighten off the birds of prey without actually harming them.

58
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,531
Most of the farmers had at least one dog,

59
00:04:08,531 --> 00:04:13,370
and said this was a big help at scaring away the predators.

60
00:04:13,370 --> 00:04:17,498
Some of the farmers also reported that during the breeding season,

61
00:04:17,498 --> 00:04:23,831
when the chickens were particularly vulnerable, they encouraged their children to watch over the chickens

62
00:04:23,831 --> 00:04:28,380
and to hit pans with a metal spoon so that the resulting noise would

63
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:33,670
succeed in driving away birds that were trying to seize the young chicks.

64
00:04:33,670 --> 00:04:36,837
None of these methods was a hundred per cent effective,

65
00:04:36,837 --> 00:04:42,388
so as a result, the village people told us that rather than just using

66
00:04:42,388 --> 00:04:46,918
one method, they were forced to use a combination for them to have any

67
00:04:46,918 --> 00:04:48,080
effect.

68
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:53,797
And even so, these birds of prey remain a major threat to the chickens’ survival

69
00:04:53,797 --> 00:04:58,150
and cause considerable economic loss to farmers.

70
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:04,380
So we looked at the possibility of a longer-term solution to …
